Widescreen scenery range: draw the level polygons the widened view shows.

Crash 2 does not decide per frame which level polygons to draw. Each camera
path carries an SLST entry, authored offline: a polygon list for every camera
node, stored as the list at node 0, a delta per node step and the list at the
last node. The camera update resolves the entry (property 0x103 of the path,
0x80014260 returning it at 0x8002037C), func_80029800 applies each step's
delta (forward: 0x8003AE54) to the current list [gp+0x214] = 0x8005F390, and
the node and path go to 0x800608E8 / 0x800608D4. func_80041E5C draws the list.

The lists hold what each node's 4:3 view sees. Across every SLST entry on the
disc, two nodes either side add 13.5% to a node's list on average (by
polygon). So any wider view - squash or native-wide - showed level scenery
appearing and vanishing at its edges: it was never sent to the renderer.

crash2_wide_slst.h (new) draws, at node n, the union of the lists of nodes
n-k..n+k. The renderer's own tests (backface, depth, and the screen test that
crash2_wide_reject.h widens in native-wide) still drop what is not on screen.

- The game's list is drawn exactly as the game built it, repeats included;
  polygons are only added, each once (a quad matched on its index: its
  variant bits are per-node draw state), nearest node first, right after the
  polygon that precedes it in the neighbour's own list. At most half as many
  again (+32), and never over the game's own 1520-entry list size.
- The lists are rebuilt here with a C port of the game's forward delta, which
  reproduces all 63,854 node lists of the 1,986 entries the Python reference
  closes (tuning/wide_slst_sim). The rebuilt list of the current node must
  equal the game's list, checked on every call, or the game's list is drawn
  untouched.
- The game's list and its buffers are never written: the merged list lives in
  runtime memory (psx_mod_memory_alloc) and only the call's $a0 points at it.
- The renderer appends primitives to a per-frame buffer (0x16400 bytes,
  allocated at 0x80016288) and never checks its end. A merged list is used
  only while the room left holds 64 bytes per added polygon plus 16 KB.
- 50 code words are checked (the entry lookup, the node walk, the stores of
  node and path, the delta, the renderer's list and primitive handling, both
  render calls, the buffer size). Identity at 4:3 and on 4:3 frames.

PSX_CRASH2_WIDE_SLST=N: nodes either side at 16:9, scaled by the live
widescreen margin like the object range (0046). The c2_slst debug command
changes it live and reports counters, carried by the heartbeat as
"wide_slst".

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake; overlay shards are unaffected.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/runtime/src/crash2_wide_slst.h
@@ -0,0 +1,554 @@
+/* SCUS-94154 only: draw the scenery the widened view shows, not just the 4:3 one.
+ *
+ * Crash 2 does not decide per frame which level polygons to draw. Each camera
+ * path carries an SLST entry, authored offline: a polygon list for every
+ * camera node, stored as the list at node 0, a delta per node step and the
+ * list at the last node. The camera update (0x80020200..0x80020830) resolves
+ * the entry (property 0x103 of the path, 0x80014260), and every node step runs
+ * func_80029800, which applies the step's delta (forward, 0x8003AE54) to the
+ * current list [gp+0x214] = 0x8005F390. The node and path then go to
+ * 0x800608E8 / 0x800608D4. func_80041E5C draws that list, polygon by polygon
+ * (ids (world<<13)|index; 0x1800 marks a quad, its variant bits draw state).
+ *
+ * The lists hold what each node's 4:3 view sees: across every level a node's
+ * neighbours add 7% (one node either side) to 14% (two) polygons to its list.
+ * So a wider view showed scenery appearing and vanishing at its edges,
+ * in squash and native-wide alike - nothing at the edge was ever sent to the
+ * renderer.
+ *
+ * This draws, at node n, the union of the lists of nodes n-k..n+k: polygons
+ * the 4:3 view at a neighbouring node sees, which is where the wider view's
+ * edges go. The renderer's own tests (backface, depth, the screen test, which
+ * crash2_wide_reject.h widens in native-wide) still reject any that are not
+ * actually on screen.
+ *
+ *   - The game's list is drawn exactly as the game built it, repeats and all;
+ *     polygons are only added, each once, nearest node first, right after the
+ *     polygon that precedes it in the neighbour's own list.
+ *   - The lists are rebuilt here from the entry with the game's forward delta
+ *     (ported from 0x8003AE54 and checked on every SLST entry of every level:
+ *     start + all deltas == end). Before anything is added, the rebuilt list
+ *     for the current node must match the game's own list; otherwise the game
+ *     is left alone (counted as a mismatch).
+ *   - The game's list and its buffers are never written. The merged list goes
+ *     to runtime memory (psx_mod_memory_alloc) and only this call's $a0
+ *     points at it.
+ *   - The renderer appends primitives to a per-frame buffer (0x16400 bytes)
+ *     without ever checking its end. Polygons are added only while the space
+ *     left can hold 64 bytes for each of them plus a reserve; otherwise this
+ *     frame draws the game's list.
+ *   - Off (identity) at 4:3 and on frames presented 4:3.
+ *
+ * PSX_CRASH2_WIDE_SLST=N: nodes either side at 16:9, scaled by the live
+ * widescreen margin like the object range (crash2_wide_spawn.h). The c2_slst
+ * debug command changes it live and reports counters; the heartbeat carries
+ * them as "wide_slst". */
+
+#define C2SL_ENTRY_RA    0x8002037Cu  /* after 0x80014260: $v0 = SLST entry  */
+#define C2SL_RENDER_FN   0x80041E5Cu
+#define C2SL_RA_SITE1    0x80011CB8u
+#define C2SL_RA_SITE2    0x80018464u
+#define C2SL_LIST_PTR    0x8005F390u  /* [gp+0x214], the current list         */
+#define C2SL_NODE        0x800608E8u
+#define C2SL_CAM         0x800608D4u
+#define C2SL_FRAME0      0x8006345Cu  /* the two frame structs, 8340 bytes    */
+#define C2SL_FRAME_SIZE  8340u
+#define C2SL_MAGIC       0x0100FFFFu
+#define C2SL_TYPE        4u
+#define C2SL_MAX_LIST    1520         /* the game's list buffers hold 1520    */
+#define C2SL_MAX_ITEMS   1025
+#define C2SL_MAX_ITEM_HW 8192         /* halfwords in one item                */
+#define C2SL_PRIM_SIZE   0x16400u     /* per-frame primitive buffer           */
+#define C2SL_PRIM_POLY   64u          /* bytes allowed per added polygon      */
+#define C2SL_PRIM_RESERVE 0x4000u
+#define C2SL_MAX_K       8
+#define C2SL_SENT        0xFFFF00
